# Third-party notices: lyrichub-align

The align plugin (`plugins/align`) is one program, `lyrichub-align.exe`, with ONNX Runtime built
in. This file lists what it contains and what it downloads, with their licenses. The Rust part
is generated with `cargo about` (see `tools/licenses/README.md`); the other sections are kept by
hand in `tools/licenses/align.hbs`. The plugin itself is licensed like LyricHub, under MIT with
the Commons Clause (`LICENSE.txt` in the ZIP).

## ONNX Runtime 1.31.0

Microsoft's ONNX Runtime runs the model. It is linked statically from the prebuilt package
that the `ort` crate fetches (CPU; the DirectML provider is compiled in but its DLL is not
shipped or used). Its own third-party notices (protobuf, Abseil, Eigen, ONNX, FlatBuffers and
more) are in `onnxruntime-ThirdPartyNotices.txt` next to this file, unchanged from
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/blob/v1.31.0/ThirdPartyNotices.txt

